            <div xml:id="d244">

                <pb facs="0627" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/1010: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-17T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                                1922—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:30
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>69. My telegram number 68, August 12, 10 a.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d244-f1"/>
                    Senate and Chamber of Deputies have given practically unanimous vote of
                    confidence to Minister for Foreign Affairs for his conduct of negotiations in
                    Washington. Early ratification probable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
